## 1. Conventions

- Screen ids are `SCR-NNN`, assigned once and never renumbered.
- Every interactive element has a stable id, used as an annotation target.
- Layouts use fenced `wireloom` blocks where available, monospace ASCII otherwise.
- Flows use Mermaid. Two gotchas: a lowercase `end` used as a node label breaks the flowchart, and a
  node label starting with `o` or `x` needs a leading space or a capital.
- States and breakpoints are defined once in [DESIGN.md](DESIGN.md) and referenced here, never
  restated.

